# The people of the Tser Pool camp (lane 28, 2026-10-08: "more people to talk to"): Old Dorina at the stew pot,
# Radu the horse-master by the pen, Petru at his grinding bench, Big Tobar mending a wheel, and Zora walking the track
# to the road. All of them answer to Stanimir, and through him to the castle; none of them will say so. They are gone
# once the camp has turned on the party (the location's `when`). Unvoiced for now: the voice thread casts them.

~ dorina
Old Dorina: Sit, sit. Nobody walks past my pot hungry, not even strangers. Strangers least of all; they never know when they'll eat next.
* What's in the pot? -> dorina_pot
* Have you been with the camp long? -> dorina_long
* We can't stay. -> END

~ dorina_pot
Old Dorina: Plums, onions, a hare Zora shot, and whatever the last pot left behind. This pot has not been empty since before Stanimir had teeth.
Narrator: She ladles out a bowl without asking. It is hot, sweet and peppery, and it is the first thing in this valley that has tasted of anything.
interject tag:blunt: That's good. That's actually good.
Old Dorina: Of course it is. Eat, and then go and see the old woman in the big tent. She has been looking at the road for you.
-> END

~ dorina_long
Old Dorina: Long enough to have buried a husband, two sisters and a horse I liked better than the husband. The road takes and the road gives. Mostly it takes.
-> dorina

~ radu
if quest.the_grey_mare and quest.the_grey_mare != rumored
-> svalich_road/grey_mare:radu
endif
Radu: Ah! Travellers with good boots and no horse. Tragic. I have a cure for that.
* What do you have? -> radu_horses
* Have you seen anyone on the road? -> radu_road
* [if flag.mare_rumor] Zora says you walked your grey to the crossroads tonight. -> svalich_road/grey_mare:asks
* Not today. -> END

~ radu_horses
if quest.the_grey_mare
-> svalich_road/grey_mare:horses_without
endif
Radu: Look at them. Plaited, brushed, fed better than the burgomaster of Vallaki. That grey one would carry you to the mountains and back and never complain.
Radu: Not for sale, of course. None of them are for sale today. But tomorrow, who knows? Come back tomorrow.
interject class:rogue: He's not selling. He's pricing us.
-> END

~ radu_road
if flag.nicu_kin_told
Radu: Nobody on the road worth knowing. Not since Nicu. We tied a ribbon for him, and the fiddle plays slow, and I have nobody to cheat at dice.
-> END
endif
if not quest.the_hanged_vistana and not flag.crossroads_gallows_seen
quest the_hanged_vistana asked
endif
Radu: Young Nicu rode out for Vallaki with a mare to sell, four days gone now. He'll be back with a new song and no money, the way he always is.
Radu: His sister watches the road for him. Don't tell her I said four days. She counts them herself.
-> END

~ petru
Narrator: The grinding wheel keeps turning under his foot. He looks at your weapons before he looks at your faces.
Petru: Good steel. Badly kept. You've been using it on things that bleed black.
* Can you sharpen our blades? -> petru_sharpen
* Who do you sharpen for? -> petru_who
* Goodbye. -> END

~ petru_sharpen
Petru: For you, no. For the camp, yes. A knife I have sharpened is a knife I know. I like to know every knife in this camp.
-> END

~ petru_who
Petru: For Stanimir. For the camp. For whoever Stanimir says.
Petru: Don't draw steel near the fire, guest. Everyone here would forget your name very quickly.
-> END

~ tobar
if quest.called_by_name and quest.called_by_name != rumored
-> svalich_road/called_by_name:tobar
endif
Narrator: A man as big as a doorway is fitting a new spoke into a cracked wheel, humming to it.
Big Tobar: Hold still, you. Hold still. There. Oh! Hello. Sorry. I was talking to the wheel.
* What happened to it? -> tobar_wheel
* Is the road east safe? -> tobar_road
* [if flag.nelu_rumor] Zora says your son went after a voice. -> svalich_road/called_by_name:asks
* Carry on. -> END

~ tobar_wheel
Big Tobar: The road to the crossroads happened to it. Roots under the mud, stones under the roots. Every wheel in this camp is half new spokes, like me.
-> END

~ tobar_road
Big Tobar: Safe? It's the Svalich Road. The wolves keep to the trees in the day, mostly. At night they keep to wherever you are.
Big Tobar: Walk in the middle. Don't stop to help anyone who calls from the trees. Even if they know your name. Especially then.
-> END

~ zora
Zora: Strangers off the road. I'll remember your faces, and how many of you there are.
* Why do you count us? -> zora_count
* Heard anything interesting? -> zora_road
* Goodbye. -> END

~ zora_count
Zora: I count everyone. People coming, people going. Most nights the numbers match.
Zora: When they don't, Stanimir wants to know which way the missing ones went.
-> END

~ zora_road
Zora: A black carriage went by two nights ago with nobody driving it. We all stood very still until it was gone. You'll want to do the same if you see it.
if not quest.the_grey_mare
set mare_rumor
quest the_grey_mare rumored
Zora: It stopped by Radu's pen. In the morning there was a purse on the gatepost, and Radu took it, and he hasn't looked anyone in the eye since.
Zora: Tonight he walked his grey down the road toward the crossroads. He came back without her. I counted.
elif flag.carriage_beaten
Zora: It went back up the castle road the other night, empty, faster than it came. I counted that too.
endif
if not quest.called_by_name
set nelu_rumor
quest called_by_name rumored
Zora: And Big Tobar's boy, Nelu. Three nights ago he stood up from the fire and said "that's Mama", and walked off toward the falls track. Tobar's wife has been dead six years. One went out. None came back. I counted.
elif flag.nelu_home
Zora: Nelu came back. The numbers match again. I like it when the numbers match.
endif
if not quest.last_muster
set muster_rumor
quest last_muster rumored
Zora: And every night after midnight, riders go east along the road toward the gates. Twelve of them. Bones on bones, horses and men. None of them ever comes back, and the next night there are twelve again. I've stopped counting them. They don't change.
elif flag.bone_marshal_beaten
Zora: No riders, these three nights. Twelve nights in a row I counted none. I miss them, a little. They were very regular.
endif
-> svalich_road/the_tinkers_wagon:zora_news

# Lane 28 (2026-10-08, "more people walking around and doing things"): Lavinia dancing on the plank stage, Iancu
# throwing knives at a stump, Old Marin skinning a deer by the trees, and the camp dog. Unvoiced for now.

~ lavinia
if level >= 3 or quest.the_dancing_bear
-> svalich_road/the_dancing_bear:lavinia
endif
Lavinia [smile]: Clap or don't, the steps are the same. My grandmother danced this for a prince once. He was dead by morning, but she said he'd enjoyed it.
-> END

~ iancu
Iancu: Ten paces. I hit the knot nine times in ten. Stanimir says that tenth one is the one that kills you. So I keep throwing.
-> END

~ marin
if quest.the_dancing_bear and quest.the_dancing_bear != done or flag.bear_trap_marked
-> svalich_road/the_dancing_bear:marin
endif
Old Marin: One deer, and I walked half the night for it. The wolves had the rest. They don't share, and nor do I, unless you're hungry. Are you hungry?
-> END

~ nelu
Nelu: I sing now, when anything calls from the trees. Badly, on purpose. Things that use your mother's voice can't stand bad singing. That's my theory.
-> END

~ dog
Narrator: The camp dog noses at your pack, finds nothing worth stealing, and wanders back to the fire to wait for Dorina to drop something.
-> END
